  "recommendation": "C_three_stage_X_CH4_N2",
  "recommendation_why": "Two-stage X+CH4 works but the CH4 evaporator sits near 6 kPa at -185 C (freeze 81.6 K), which starves evaporation rate. Two-stage X+N2 has only ~17 K between X freeze and N2 crit, so HX dT is tight and freeze risk is real. Three-stage X / CH4 / N2 opens both windows, keeps N2 evaporator at a usable tens-of-kPa, and makes the N2 condenser the LN2 tap."
